      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 360 turntable (MiniMax H3 + 360 orbit LoRA)\n\nOne character image becomes a looping 360° camera orbit, its 72 frames as transparent PNGs, and an 8-view sheet.\n\n**How it works**\n\n- The input is scaled and center-cropped to 768 x 768, BiRefNet cuts the subject out, and it is pasted on a flat grey backdrop.\n- The official H3 image-to-video route (`MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo`) gets that image as **first and last frame**; pablodawson's 360 orbit LoRA turns the camera once around the frozen subject and lands on the start frame.\n- 73 frames at 24 fps; the last frame repeats the first, so the loop keeps frames 0-71. BiRefNet cuts every loop frame out (RGBA).\n- The sheet takes frames 0, 9, 18 ... 63 of the loop: 45° steps along the orbit, 4 x 2. Which way the camera turns is the LoRA's; check frame 18 before you label the views.\n\n**Settings** (the LoRA card's): 768 x 768, 73 frames, 28 steps, LoRA strength 1.0, no CFG, the prompt verbatim. Frame indices assume 73 frames; with another length, pick at (length - 1) / 8 steps and set the loop length to length - 1.\n\n**Faster, unverified:** un-bypass the LightX2V 4-step Turbo LoRA, add `MiniMaxH3SigmaShift` 6/3 after it for the guider and the scheduler, and set the scheduler to 4 steps.\n\n**Models and nodes:** model sets `minimax-h3-i2v`, `minimax-h3-utilities` (orbit and Turbo LoRAs), `utility-tools` (BiRefNet); core nodes only.\n\n**Licence:** H3 and the orbit LoRA are under the MiniMax H3 Community License; check its terms before you ship the output in a product.\n\nOrbit LoRA: [pablodawson/MiniMax-H3-360-Orbit-LoRA](https://huggingface.co/pablodawson/MiniMax-H3-360-Orbit-LoRA/blob/5ddbc2dbbe95edbbdaf5017c3e934b1d01791697/README.md).\n"
      ],
      "title": "Read me"
    },
